<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59452" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κουρ-εῶτις</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέρα</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἑορτή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.46
				</span></i>
			), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, ἡ, the third day of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπατούρια</span>, on which children were presented to the
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φράτερες</span>, and boys competed in
			recitation, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				21b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κ. Ἀπατουρίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1237.28
				</span></i>
			. (Perh. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κείρω, κουρά</span>,
			because the child's hair is said to have been cut on that day, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
